#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a560db4d-e9d3-5d89-b2cd-c886f32db9df" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Third Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d47d315-fd39-5905-91d6-6c076260040d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d47d315-fd39-5905-91d6-6c076260040d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242430} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbf8899-710c-5264-b7a5-b0a51ef658f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242429}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "847a1127-b379-55f0-bcc6-f21c519a7a9e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-319517" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-8-5\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/c598c3b872cd2c4b3af08d8b2dbaf6a79512fe382473320feb526f31e5ece246.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{5}{8})=0.558\\,599…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi +0.558\\,599…≈3.70,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a560db4d-e9d3-5d89-b2cd-c886f32db9df" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Third Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de0ed0cf-1d97-569c-a057-ee624747eaab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242433} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ebed28-0492-5f2d-9c60-07b9616962f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de0ed0cf-1d97-569c-a057-ee624747eaab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242433} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b8fa78-aa93-597b-835f-b55c9802a212" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242432}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "784bc253-6dac-5f97-b706-d2c329fefc85" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-319519" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-11-6\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/ab2f3a9137c05ca19507e44d2bb2ef4b369c762189019265d8fe3bad34822fe7.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{6}{11})=0.499\\,346…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi +0.499\\,346…≈3.64,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Fourth Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae3a11fe-83f7-51f8-a2b6-a312fc040f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242437} {:answer/id #uuid "bc94e163-e45a-5377-8083-3174d29e19d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc94e163-e45a-5377-8083-3174d29e19d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242438} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa1482a9-41f5-5769-ad7b-35fb1250adb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242436}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46ec1ca3-4689-5158-9a8c-aaa28f0d5a07" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-319581" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=8\\sqrt{3}-8\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/78399e67e0ba69c1d7848a41aa5d4a5f8040fc578aab30a99f7e19ac86ece179.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{8\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833ac63c-235b-5059-ab7c-56eb1e44d79e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Second Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4439b33b-d0dc-584e-bf17-75abccae95ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242441} {:answer/id #uuid "21b98ea1-a4d8-56dc-81d4-2476c276adf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242442} {:answer/id #uuid "8a21fbbb-d371-51b9-be2d-3daefcb68885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242443} {:answer/id #uuid "e55d2641-8c5e-5ecd-8563-264a2982b09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242444} {:answer/id #uuid "629fbaf2-2c6d-55d1-9b71-70c01a308e3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e55d2641-8c5e-5ecd-8563-264a2982b09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242444} :answer-field/id #uuid "23a6f6e5-5519-5213-b609-1da104a9ecf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242440}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "182ca814-357c-5897-88e6-eaddeb481aa4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-8257" :question/problem "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-3+4\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/373ea8254a9816f67bfbcaf993348f409c1047284d09c43e5d41e68b15c5af58.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & ≈0.927\\,30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)≈\\pi -0.927\\,30≈2.21\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Fourth Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fed38372-dbad-59d6-b4e1-d1ce198fc679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087199} {:answer/id #uuid "2402ae36-8c33-5dea-a1f8-0c71d29869b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087200} {:answer/id #uuid "30043cab-ba72-546d-b917-1eafd75bbef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087201} {:answer/id #uuid "31b44cda-0b0b-576d-8f79-af288d1a0400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087202} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdd86ad-3200-5c79-98b3-9069d63fb372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fdd86ad-3200-5c79-98b3-9069d63fb372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087203} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc95eff5-2024-5abe-aa4e-bffc546c8770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087198}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1eede2a0-b32f-5395-87d1-df0fef1f0013" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-8454" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z = 7 - 5\\textrm{i}$.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[MATH: [0, 2π).]$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/d096d76118bc06b2d5c79d5017c0178d96fc84bff6f97d563b7b872d26e75d20.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{5}{7})≈0.620\\,25.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.620\\,25≈5.66\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}]}
